zig-out/
zig-cache/
.zig-cache/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib

# Crash dumps. FreeBSD writes <progname>.core into the cwd, so the name follows
# whichever binary died -- build.core, test.core, securearc.core. A single filename
# only ever blocks the crash that has already happened: build.core was listed here
# after one landed in a commit on 2026-07-26, and test.core walked straight past it
# on 2026-07-29 because the failing binary had a different name. Cores are tens of
# megabytes and can hold key material lifted from process memory, so match the
# pattern.
*.core

# Python bytecode from the RFC 7208 conformance harness. A .pyc was committed on
# 2026-07-29 for want of this line -- same class as the *.core lapse: a build
# artefact ignored by filename rather than by pattern.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The conformance harness virtualenv: thousands of third-party files, rebuilt from
# requirements.txt in one command. test/rfc7208/README.md tells you to create it
# right here, so `git status` offered to add the whole tree the first time the
# suite was run from a clean checkout. Already listed in securearc for the same
# reason; this daemon was missed.
.venv/
